---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy — One Reader" description="One Reader privacy information.">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="shell max-w-3xl min-h-[70vh] py-20 sm:py-28">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-5">Privacy notice · implementation draft</p>
    <h1 class="section-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="brand-prose mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
      One Reader is designed to collect as little as possible. This notice makes the consent choices visible for the free account and the separate optional Journal messages.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-10 border-t border-border pt-10 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-x-12">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.005em]">What we collect</h2>
        <p class="brand-prose mt-4 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Your email address, month and year of birth, languages, account and subscription status, and the communication preferences you selected. We do not ask for your day of birth, and the Journal preference is stored separately from service registration.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.005em]">Why we use it</h2>
        <p class="brand-prose mt-4 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">To operate the account, match members who can correspond in the same language, and keep the 14–17 and adult matching pools separate. Journal notes and product news are sent only when you choose the separate optional checkbox.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.005em]">Legal bases</h2>
        <p class="brand-prose mt-4 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">The service account is needed to operate correspondence. Journal notes and product news use a separate optional consent, and these purposes are never bundled into one required acceptance.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="rights">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.005em]">Your controls</h2>
        <p class="brand-prose mt-4 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">You can withdraw optional Journal consent, request access, correct inaccurate information or ask for deletion. Birth details are locked in the account to protect the matching pools, but you can request a correction if they are inaccurate.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.005em]">When a letter is reported</h2>
        <p class="brand-prose mt-4 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">The correspondence is closed and the reported letter, already stored in encrypted form, can be made available to One Reader for a separate human review. We record the reporting member, the letter and the selected category; the form does not ask for additional free-text details.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.005em]">When you close your account</h2>
        <p class="brand-prose mt-4 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Your service access and incoming deliveries stop as soon as you request deletion. We retain only the minimum records needed to process the request or handle a related dispute for up to 30 days. Records subject to a longer legal obligation, such as billing evidence, remain only for that obligation and are then removed.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-border pt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.005em]">Operational principles</h2>
      <ul class="brand-prose mt-5 grid gap-3 leading-7 text-muted-foreground sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-x-12">
        <li>Mailbox ownership may be confirmed with a double opt-in link.</li>
        <li>No tracking pixels or open tracking in correspondence emails.</li>
        <li>Consent records are purpose-specific, versioned and timestamped.</li>
        <li>Data is deleted when its purpose and retention period end.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
